des wait no longer than four hours to start.  GPU nodes are reserved for th=
e purchasing Project=E2=80=99s dedicated use. If the node type or configura=
tion you are looking for is not listed, you can request a custom node purch=
ase.</p>
<p>Access to compute nodes is purchased for a specified number of years aft=
er which access expires.  When Priority Access compute resources expire at =
the end of the purchased access period, user access to those resources is r=
evoked.</p>
<section id=3D"custom-hardware">
<span id=3D"priority-custom-hardware"></span><h4>Custom Hardware<a class=3D=
"headerlink" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/res=
ources/quest-resource.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#custom-hardware" title=
=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h4>
<p>GPU and high-memory nodes that are not in stock are custom node requests=
. When requesting a custom node, please provide as many hardware and techni=
cal details as possible so that we can investigate options and generate a p=
rice quote for the node.  RCDS will contact you to discuss your requirement=
s. Custom compute nodes take 3=E2=80=936 months for ordering, fulfillment, =
and implementation.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"priority-access-storage">
<span id=3D"quest-priority-storage"></span><h3>Priority Access Storage<a cl=
ass=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/que=
st/resources/quest-resource.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#priority-access-s=
torage" title=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
<p>Storage can be purchased by the terabyte for a specified number of years=
.  The storage is set up in a directory in the <a class=3D"reference intern=
al" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/f=
ilesystem/filesystem.html#allocation-directories"><span class=3D"std std-re=
f">projects space</span></a>.  A Project can have both General Access and P=
riority Access storage resources, but they cannot be directly combined; eac=
h resource type will have its own directory and account identifier.</p>
<p>When Priority Access storage expires, the Project=E2=80=99s storage dire=
ctory quota is reduced by the amount of storage that is expiring. For examp=
le, if you=E2=80=99ve made multiple storage purchases totaling 10 TB, and a=
 purchase for 2 TB expires, the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate=
"><span class=3D"pre">/projects/&lt;account_id&gt;</span></code> directory =
quota will be set to 8 TB.  If the total amount of data in that directory e=
xceeds the new quota, attempts to write new files to the directory will res=
ult in disk full errors.  The storage in the directory must be reduced belo=
w the new quota to continue to use the storage directory.  If the entirety =
of your Priority Access storage quota expires, the quota will be reduced to=
 0 TB and any remaining data will be deleted 90 days after expiration.</p>
<p>Like all projects storage, Priority Access storage limits the total numb=
er of files to 10,000 files per GB of purchased quota. When Priority Access=
 storage expires and the quota is reduced, the file count limit is reduced =
proportionally as well.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"classroom-resources">
<span id=3D"id2"></span><h2>Classroom Resources<a class=3D"headerlink" href=
=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/resources/quest-reso=
urce.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#classroom-resources" title=3D"Link to th=
is heading">#</a></h2>
<p>Classroom resources on Quest are available to support both official Nort=
hwestern courses and training events or workshops sponsored by Northwestern=
 faculty or staff.</p>
<p>Project Sponsors, Leads, and Managers are responsible for adding and rem=
oving students from the classroom resources. Please request resources at le=
ast one week in advance to ensure that the resources are active in time for=
 the class or workshop. Students will be notified when they have been added=
 to the resources.</p>
<p>Sponsors, Leads, and Managers are also responsible for teaching students=
 how to use the Quest resources necessary for the class or workshop. This i=
ncludes logging in, transferring files to and from Quest, use of software, =
package installation and management, and, if needed, how to submit jobs. Sp=
onsors, Leads, and Managers are responsible for fielding initial questions =
or issues. If you encounter an error with the system, please submit a help =
request to <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"mailto:quest-help%40nort=
hwestern.edu" target=3D"_blank">quest-help<span>@</span>northwestern<span>.=
</span>edu <svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D=
"0 0 16 16" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-a=
